**Why it could work**: 4 consecutive local layers create a "global context desert" where full-sequence information degrades through recurrence decay. Interleaving global layers at positions 2 and 5 refreshes full-sequence attention every 2 layers instead of letting it degrade for 4.

**Why it might not**: If the cross-chunk recurrence already provides adequate long-range context, the global refresh is redundant.

